	<dc:title xml:lang="en">Fast Multivariate Power Series Multiplication in Characteristic Zero</dc:title>
	<dc:title xml:lang="es">Fast Multivariate Power Series Multiplication in Characteristic Zero</dc:title>
	<dc:creator xml:lang="es">Lecerf, G.</dc:creator>
	<dc:creator xml:lang="es">Schost, E.</dc:creator>
	<dc:subject xml:lang="en">Multivariate power series</dc:subject>
	<dc:subject xml:lang="en">fast multiplication</dc:subject>
	<dc:subject xml:lang="en">complexity</dc:subject>
	<dc:subject xml:lang="es">Multivariate power series</dc:subject>
	<dc:subject xml:lang="es">fast multiplication</dc:subject>
	<dc:subject xml:lang="es">complexity</dc:subject>
	<dc:description xml:lang="en">Let k be a field of characteristic zero. We present a fast algorithm for multiplying multivariate power series over k truncated in total degree. Up to logarithmic factors, its complexity is optimal, i.e. linear in the number of coeffcients of the series.</dc:description>
	<dc:description xml:lang="es">Let k be a field of characteristic zero. We present a fast algorithm for multiplying multivariate power series over k truncated in total degree. Up to logarithmic factors, its complexity is optimal, i.e. linear in the number of coeffcients of the series.</dc:description>
